<title>NETHERLANDS: Dutch central bank allocates fresh liquidity.</title>
<headline>Dutch central bank allocates fresh liquidity.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Dutch central bank said it allocated 2.80 billion guilders to the money market under a seven-day special advances pact at an unchanged rate of 2.50 percent.</p>
<p>Individual banks' applications up to 3.50 billion guilders were met for 10.5 percent. Above that level no subscriptions were awarded.</p>
<p>The pact replaces a seven-day facility of 2.86 billion guilders which expired today.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsdesk +31 20 504 5000</p>
